      "intel_summary": "All 5 of the top failed-login source IPs have a 'malicious' reputation. Specifically, 198.51.100.77 and 198.51.100.23 are associated with known host-scanning/brute-force ranges, while 203.0.113.141, 203.0.113.51, and 203.0.113.23 are linked to distributed credential-stuffing botnet activity.",
      "enrichment_notes": "The threat intelligence significantly increases the severity of this incident. The initial evidence already indicated a potential brute-force or credential-stuffing attack with a high volume of failed logins across many distinct IPs and targeted usernames. The intelligence lookup confirms that *all* the top source IPs involved in these failed logins are known malicious actors, specifically associated with scanning, brute-forcing, and botnet activities. This confirms the malicious nature of the observed activity and suggests a well-orchestrated attack by established bad actors rather than benign errors or a single-source attempt. The presence of botnet-related IPs further suggests a distributed and potentially more persistent threat.",
